      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Emit the driver report outside pytest capture**\n\nIn the Modal path, `ci/torch_latest.py:739-748` invokes pytest with `--verbose` but not `-s`; `pytest --help` documents `-s` as the shortcut for `--capture=no` and says captured output is shown for failed tests. Because this test normally passes, the printed driver version is suppressed and therefore does not become visible in the CI log as intended. Emit it as an unconditional controller command before pytest or explicitly disable capture for the probe.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.",
      "commit_id": "9275430cca20c5f1bd0e23d4995d2c3e54e6eece",
      "created_at": "2026-10-14T06:57:54Z",
      "diff_hunk": "@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@\n+# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n+# DeepSpeed Team\n+\"\"\"Diagnostic probe: surface host GPU driver details in CI logs.\n+\n+The modal-torch-latest Sandbox report step does not print the host driver\n+version, which hid a fleet-wide driver update (610.57.04) that intermittently\n+poisons CUDA contexts. This probe makes the driver version visible in test\n+logs so future infra regressions are attributable at a glance.\n+\"\"\"\n+\n+import subprocess\n+\n+import pytest\n+\n+\n+def _driver_version() -> str:\n+    result = subprocess.run([\"nvidia-smi\", \"--query-gpu=driver_version,name\", \"--format=csv,noheader\"],\n+                            capture_output=True,\n+                            text=True,\n+                            check=True)\n+    return result.stdout.strip()\n+\n+\n+def test_report_host_driver_version():\n+    print(f\"DS_CI_DRIVER_PROBE: {_driver_version()}\")",
